# Maps each convention file to the plugin(s) its skill references require.
# A convention is "satisfied" when at least one of the listed plugins is
# linked under ~/.claude/skills/. Pipe-separate alternatives (any one is
# enough); separate independent deps with additional lines for the same file
# if it needs multiple plugins.
#
# Only conventions that actively direct Claude to load or use a specific skill
# are listed here — conventions that merely mention a skill as optional reading
# are omitted. Missing-plugin warnings in check-companions.sh use this file.
#
# Format: convention-filename:plugin-name-or-pipe-separated-alternatives

fetch-execute-installs.md:dfadler-agent-config
focus-stealing.md:dfadler-agent-config|detached-terminal
vite-plugin.md:vite
git-worktree-usage.md:dfadler-agent-config|worktree-core
visual-verification.md:dfadler-agent-config|pr-visual-capture
